example.paragraph:
The set $S = \left\{ \mathbf{u}_{1}\text{,~}\mathbf{u}_{2}\text{,~}\mathbf{u}_{3} \right\}$ in Example 1 is an orthogonal basis for $\text{ℝ}^{3}$. Express the vector $\textbf{y} = \left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      6 \\
      1 \\
      {- 8}
      \end{array} \right\rbrack$ as a linear combination of the vectors in $S$.

content.paragraph:
